  "rule": {
    "title": "Polite complaints and requests",
    "explanation": "En inglés las peticiones y las quejas suenan más educadas si las suavizamos. Unas cuantas fórmulas:\n- Para empezar: «I'm sorry to bother you, but…», «Excuse me, could I…?»\n- Para dar una mala noticia: «I'm afraid…» (me temo que…)\n- Para pedir algo: «Could you…?», «Would you…?», «Do you think you could…?»\n- «Would you mind» + «-ing»? (¿le importaría…?)\n- Para pedir permiso: «Could I…?», «Do you mind if I…?»\n\nEjemplos:\n- «I'm sorry to bother you, but the shower doesn't work.»\n- «I'm afraid there's no hot water.»\n- «Would you mind changing our room?»\n- «Do you think you could send someone?»\n\nOjo con «Would you mind…?» y «Do you mind if…?»: si quieres decir que no te importa, respondes «Not at all» o «No, go ahead» (no, en absoluto). «Yes» significaría que sí te importa.\n\nPara agradecer y disculparse:\n- «That's very kind of you.»\n- «I'm so sorry about that.»",
    "table": {
      "headers": [
        "Para…",
        "Fórmula",
        "Ejemplo"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Empezar",
          "I'm sorry to bother you, but…",
          "I'm sorry to bother you, but the TV doesn't work."
        ],
        [
          "Mala noticia",
          "I'm afraid…",
          "I'm afraid the room is too noisy."
        ],
        [
          "Pedir",
          "Could you…?",
          "Could you change our room?"
        ],
        [
          "Pedir (más educado)",
          "Would you mind + -ing?",
          "Would you mind opening the window?"
        ],
        [
          "Permiso",
          "Do you mind if I…?",
          "Do you mind if I sit here?"
        ],
        [
          "Responder que no importa",
          "Not at all.",
          "Would you mind? — Not at all."
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
